(footprint "UM232H"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "FTDI UM232H USB Hi-Speed FT232H dev module -- 28-pin (2x14, 0.6in/15.24mm row spacing, 2.54mm pitch) THT DIP-style module, plugs into a standard 0.6in 28-pin DIP socket. Geometry derived directly from DS_UM232H.pdf Figure 3 (Module Dimensions): pin field is 33.02mm (13 x 2.54mm) long, starting 10.0mm from the USB-connector end of the 44.5mm-long, 18.25mm-wide board -- pin1 of each row sits at Y=-16.51 (10.0mm in from the top/USB-connector edge at Y=-26.51), pin14 at Y=+16.51 (1.48mm shy of the far edge at Y=+17.99). J2 is the left row (x=-7.62), J1 is the right row (x=+7.62), matching the module's own silkscreened orientation in Figure 2 (USB connector at top, J2 left/J1 right). Pad numbers are the datasheet's own J1-n/J2-n designators -- must match the UM232H symbol's pin numbers exactly. Drill/pad sized generously (1.0mm/1.8mm) for the module's 0.5mm round pins in a socket mount. Decorative/mechanical details shown in Fig 2/3 but not part of the J1/J2 signal interface (the extra unlabeled GND through-hole and crystal-shaped silkscreen icon near the bottom of the real board) are intentionally omitted.")
	(tags "FTDI UM232H FT232H USB DIP module")
	(property "Reference" "REF**"
